Z||000002||DJRice||05-30-2001||10:03 PM||||I guess Cliff must have deleted the post because it was a false alarm.  I posted the link because that particular virus is a known hoax and that file will be found on any machine that has Windows 95/98.<P>It seems that there are just as many virus hoaxes going around as there are viruses.  Everyone assumes that because they see a warning in an email that it is valid.  I recommend bookmarking the link below and checking out any virus warning you receive against this list before you go deleting stuff off of your hard drive.<P>The "sulfnbk" virus is at the top of the hoax list currently.<P> <A HREF="http://www.icsalabs.com/html/communities/antivirus/hoaxes.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.icsalabs.com/html/communities/antivirus/hoaxes.shtml</A>  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JSocha||05-31-2001||12:41 AM||||Thanks DJ!<P>Wanted it for work.  Some of our employees have been receiving Hoax emails (including myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> ) at home as well as at work.  Some employees have taken the liberty at work, on their own, of erasing the reported files without informing me (which is what I get paid for but can't monitor every email that comes to them).  Then I end up trying to fix what they broke.<P>Like little kids with their hands behind their back:  "What did you do prior to this?"<P>Response:  "Nothing...." <P>Arrrrrgggghhhhh!<P>Now they can bookmark this page and be responsible since they don't feel it is necessary to call me when they get the alert and I don't.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||loafer87gt||05-31-2001||03:51 AM||||Yeah, it was a false virus alert. The message said to look in your in windows directory for a certain file name, and that if it was there your computer would be pooched on June 1. It said to delete the file if you had it on your machine, but the file is NEEDED by windows to handle long file names, so deleting it would screw up your machine. The virus warning itself was the actually the virus.||||reg||1
